# ── Android App Links verification ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Serve the verification file at its required path (/.well-known/assetlinks.json)
# from a NON-hidden root file, so a drag-and-drop deploy — which silently omits
# hidden dot-folders — still publishes it.
# 200 = transparent rewrite (no HTTP redirect), which Android's verifier requires.
/.well-known/assetlinks.json   /assetlinks.json   200

# ── Tidy per-app URLs ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Privacy, terms, deletion and support are ONE page each covering both apps, with
# a ?app= selector. These aliases mean the nested form works too, so a store
# listing, an email or an old link can use either shape:
#     /tutors/privacy  ==  /privacy?app=tutor
/tutors/privacy          /privacy?app=tutor          301
/tutors/terms            /terms?app=tutor            301
/tutors/delete-account   /delete-account?app=tutor   301
/tutors/support          /support?app=tutor          301
/tutors/contact          /support?app=tutor          301

# Singular and near-miss spellings of the tutor page — cheap to support, and these
# are the URLs people type after hearing the name said out loud.
/tutor        /tutors   301
/tutoring     /tutors   301
/for-tutors   /tutors   301

# Common aliases for the support page.
/contact   /support   301
/help      /support   301

# ── Tutor browser sign-in ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The tutor web app is served from this same site at /tutors/app/ (assembled by
# tools/build_site.sh). /tutors/login is kept as a stable alias because it is
# already linked from elsewhere and reads better when said out loud.
#
# No SPA rewrite is needed: the app uses hash routing (/tutors/app/#/practice/…),
# so deep links never reach the server.
/tutors/login    /tutors/app/    301
/tutor-login     /tutors/app/    301
